We also discussed lots of goodies for another day:

1) `IIndicator.WarmUp()` to skip the need to manually warm up anything or next best: `algorithm.WarmUpIndicator(indicator)`

2) Removing the need for symbolData entirely by designing mostly around the updated events; 
```
var signal = fast.Over(slow);
signal.Updated += (sender, current) => {  do logic, if detect cross, fire insight event }
```

3) Adding `IIndicator.WarmUpPeriod` -- so we know easily how many points an indicator requires to get warmed.
